Reject crafted group descriptors and a zero mkfs block size

Backport of three memory-safety fixes from the Aladdin-R-D/lwext4 fork
(https://github.com/Aladdin-R-D/lwext4), carried until lwext4 or the
osvunikernel fork picks them up.  The error codes are normalized here to
match ext4_extent.c (EIO for a corrupt on-disk value found at mount,
EINVAL for a bad mkfs argument) rather than the fork's ENXIO/EFAULT/ENOMEM.

- 2f5714d42 (out-of-bounds write in the block and inode bitmap init):
  bit_max and inodes_per_group come straight from the group descriptor
  and superblock, so a crafted image can drive ext4_bmap_bit_set() and
  the memset() past the end of the one-block bitmap buffer.  Bound both
  against the block size before touching the buffer.  Not covered by the
  extent/superblock checks already in this PR.
- 1d32b2f17 (NULL dereference in ext4_dir_en_get_name_len): guard the
  directory entry pointer in this hot untrusted dir-read helper.
- fa299459e (division by zero in create_fs_aux_info): reject a zero
  block size before dividing by it in the mkfs path.

Applies to osvunikernel/lwext4 6f6d8f7c509da696e71e80cc5a59abfc48e4971b.

